    "note": "Permit inventory by project. Status values: Approved (issued); Under Review (filed and pending); Not Filed (project is docketed at NRC and the permit is firmly required, but the application has not yet been submitted); Pre-Application (no NRC docket yet, but the permit is anticipated and the project is engaged with the agency); Projected (no NRC docket; project is at conceptual / pre-application stage and the permit is forecast based on standard reactor configurations); GAP (status not publicly available); N/A (not applicable). The Not Filed vs. Projected distinction tracks NRC docketing — Long Mott (docketed) carries Not Filed for unfiled state permits; Last Energy and TAMU (no docket) carry Projected. Critical Path = permit governs project go/no-go timing. agency_target_days = typical processing time published by the issuing agency, NOT a statutory deadline. Texas permits in this dataset do not have hard statutory clocks."
